      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": " Edward Carey Property is delighted to present this fantastic country style cottage, standing on an acre of grounds having a westerly rear aspect. \n\nWelcome to Meadow Cottage, a spectacular country-style detached residence delivering a premium ?700k+ Dublin footprint for a fraction of the cost. Spanning a generous 193 sq.m (2,077 sq.ft) of pristine, turnkey living space, this home stands on an expansive, exceptionally maintained 1-acre private oasis. Perfectly positioned for the modern professional, it balances tranquil rural living with seamless, rapid connectivity to the capital.\nAvoid the daily city rush without sacrificing your career. Meadow Cottage is equipped with high-speed fibre broadband and features a fully dedicated, bright, and quiet ground-floor home office (Bedroom 3). When you do need to commute, you are just 3 kms from Clonard village, 8 kms from Enfield town centre, and under 35 minutes from the Lucan M50 interchange via the M4. Commuter rail access from Enfield Train Station or direct Bus Éireann links from the village make hybrid working effortless.\nMoving inside, Meadow Cottage offers a delightfully unique and individual layout that provides a refreshing change from the norm. Architecturally distinct and wonderfully quirky, the flow of the home is full of character and may not suit everyone, but for those looking to escape standard cookie-cutter estate designs, it offers an incomparable, bespoke lifestyle. All doors are solid wood with rich wood flooring, this property delivers a tactile sense of craftsmanship and durability rarely found in modern developments.\nThe heart of this warm family home is a beautiful, light-filled country kitchen boasting solid wood worktops, a central island unit, and a bespoke walk-in larder/utility space that opens directly onto a sunny, west-facing rear patio. Unwind in the grand living room, featuring solid wood flooring and a beautiful brick-surround wood-burning stove.\nThe ground floor offers immense flexibility with two large double bedrooms (one perfect as a private guest room adjacent to the main family bathroom) alongside the dedicated home office.\nThe entire first floor is dedicated to luxury. The master suite is a true sanctuary, featuring a massive double bedroom, a spacious walk-in wardrobe, and a private en-suite with underfloor heating. Double doors open onto a magnificent, dual-aspect private balcony, the perfect, peaceful spot for a morning coffee overlooking your own private grounds.\nThe external grounds are a paradise for children and gardening enthusiasts alike, featuring a mature array of planting, shrubs, and established fruit trees on a secure, manicured 1-acre plot. The property also includes a substantial block-built detached garage and a heavy-duty steel shed, offering endless storage, home gym, classic car storage, workshop or detached teenage games room potential. With an expansive layout and private boundaries, there is ample room to erect horse stables or a paddock, offering a true equestrian lifestyle opportunity.\nWhile warm, inviting, and completely ready to walk into today, the home?s oil-fired central heating makes it a prime candidate for the enhanced SEAI energy upgrade grants of up to 12,500 eoro. Buyers can seamlessly transition the home to an A/B rating using low-interest 2.99% government-backed home energy loans, unlocking a discounted Green Mortgage rate post-purchase.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the sheer scale, privacy, and lifestyle value on offer.\n\nAre you bidding on one of our properties, new to the market, unsure of the procedure? Check out my website https;//www.edcarey.ie/useful-information/ for a helpful guide on buying & selling with us.\n\nTo bid on this property, please go to my website www.edcarey.ie, find the listing & hit the 'Offr' button to bring you to the registration field. I'll then approve your registration and you can bid at your convenience. \n\nOutside \ntarmacadam driveway & parking to the house. Great range of out offices including large block-built garage, large steel shed & garden shed all included. Extensive c1 acre grounds all exceptionally maintained"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (5.14m x 2.34m) spacious entrance hall with solid wood flooring & useful under-stairs storage<br>Living Room (5.14m x 5.08m) central living room with solid wood T&G flooring, solid fuel wood burning stove with attractive brick surround, curtains/blinds included <br>Dining Area (5.14m x 2.18m) <br>Kitchen (4.61m x 3.45m) lovely country style kitchen with tiled flooring, great range of fitted kitchen cabinets and island unit having solid wood worktop, appliances included<br>Utility Room (2.34m x 1.92m) plumbed for washing machine & drier & walk-in larder store<br>Bedroom 1 (3.85m x 3.32m) with solid wood T&G flooring, curtains/blinds included, large walk-in wardrobe <br>Storage (3.04m x 1.18m) <br>En-suite (2.30m x 1.68m) well-appointed en-suite with shower, wc & whb, with underfloor heating<br>Bedroom 2 (3.45m x 3.32m) ideal guest bedroom with laminate wood flooring, sliderobe wardrobe included, curtains/blinds included<br>Bathroom (2.40m x 2.28m) adjacent the guest bedroom with tiled floor & walls, bath, wc, whb & walk-in shower & radiator/towel warmer<br>Bedroom 3 (5.00m x 3.56m) with solid wood T&G flooring, blinds included. Currently in use as home-office<br>Landing (3.65m x 2.34m) large bright landing/seating area with patio doors to the balcony<br>Master Bedroom (5.69m x 5.25m) fantastic master suite with solid wood flooring, walk-in wardrobe/dressing area<br>En-suite (2.40m x 2.29m) well-appointed en-suite bathroom with shower, wc & whb & underfloor heating"
      },
